 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ef386942-0ca5-46f0-9e13-b07699f03163",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Executive Summary\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "a0f7e744-fe17-4950-b9d2-acb0003e3efd",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Monitoring deforestation across vast, remote rainforest is costly and slow. Using open Landsat‑8 imagery we tuned a MobileNetV3‑Large classifier, a proof‑of‑concept system to automatically identify common drivers in the Congo Basin. The classes trained & evaluated are: \n",
    "\n",
    "Selective logging, tropical fruit tree plantations, maize plantations, wildfire and a negative class - undisturbed forest. \n",
    "\n",
    "On an unseen test set the model achieved a macro‑averaged F1 score of 0.86. The pipeline integrates data quality checks (cloud and corruption filtering, duplicate removal), targeted class consolidation, and feature engineering to make the task tractable. The result is a replicable, low‑cost approach that can scale regional monitoring and help direct conservation resources."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4f095780-6523-4e6c-a09e-03bc3aab0506",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Background"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "2c7d4c2c-8bdb-4107-82f9-4c8bd14ce4de",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Governments and NGOs are investing heavily to curb emissions and biodiversity loss. Rainforests are high‑leverage carbon sinks but remain vulnerable due to economic incentives and limited visibility on the ground. Open satellite data now provides near‑continuous coverage; pairing it with computer vision enables affordable, repeatable monitoring of region‑specific deforestation drivers."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "54ddb3f1-8cec-4346-b259-8899ddb6e489",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Problem Statement"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "f6ba92a5-6e47-40b0-bac3-8a578bf7e0f7",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Conservation programs in Central Africa lack a scalable way to distinguish which activities are driving forest loss at regional scale. Global models underperform on local idiosyncrasies. Manual surveys and drones are expensive and slow. Public imagery is abundant but noisy—clouds, artifacts, and label issues degrade downstream models. A practical, low‑cost pipeline is needed to turn open EO data into accurate, driver‑level intelligence for the Congo Basin."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1007684b-643b-4080-b933-abbe75f3168d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Summary of Findings"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "330efc27-8f1f-4673-9fa0-b945830cfe39",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "-A lightweight CNN (MobileNetV3‑Large) fine‑tuned on Landsat‑8 RGB+NIR can separate undisturbed forest from four driver classes with macro F1 = 0.86.\n",
    "\n",
    "-Data cleaning was crucial cloud masking, corruption filtering, duplicate removal, and class consolidation improve learnability and stability.\n",
    "\n",
    "-Adding a robust negative class (undisturbed forest) from Earth Engine improves generalization.\n",
    "\n",
    "-Grad‑CAM confirms the model relies on ecologically sensible patterns (edges/streaks adjacent to canopy change; crop greenness, etc.).\n",
    "\n",
    "-Biggest limiter currently is sample size for some drivers as performance appears to scale with support."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "22d10b82-8249-4b1b-b058-4acb2b942d7b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Scope"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "40f8584e-2170-47ff-9915-7fe3f71547d4",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "This work builds off of the labelling work done by Debus et al at the university of cambridge.\n",
    "Their paper should be considered the main prerequisite to understand this project , link here https://doi.org/10.1038/s41597-024-03384-z\n",
    "\n",
    "Included: Landsat‑8 tiles (5×5 km) over the African rainforest domain (11°E–30°E, 5°S–5.5°N); years 2015–2025; RGB+NIR bands; five classes—undisturbed forest, selective logging, tropical fruit tree plantation, maize plantation, wildfire. \n",
    "\n",
    "Excluded: Drivers with insufficient support or non‑learnable signatures in this modality at 30 m (i.e hunting, catch‑all “other” classes)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "48eed200-2d1d-448c-be4f-57f1d45b10fb",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Approach"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "37f18ed4-a538-4cc0-9720-c8b32b999454",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Seed dataset: Deforestation driver tiles curated for Cameroon, provided by Debus et al\n",
    "\n",
    "Quality filtering: Threshold‑based cloud mask (Blue high / NIR low), removal of imagery with line‑drop artifacts, and down‑sampling of near‑duplicate tiles.\n",
    "\n",
    "Feature engineering: Consolidated visually similar tree‑crop classes into Tropical Fruit Tree Plantation; added 338 Undisturbed forest tiles via Google Earth Engine filtered by intact‑forest masks, date, and low cloud cover.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Modeling\n",
    "\n",
    "Backbone: MobileNetV3‑Large initialized on ImageNet; classification head remapped to 5 classes.\n",
    "\n",
    "Preprocessing: Bilinear resize to 256×256, random crop to 224×224, per‑channel normalization; random rotations during training.\n",
    "\n",
    "Training: Four stratified folds; initial LR 3e‑5 with ReduceLROnPlateau (factor 0.1 after 4 epochs without val‑loss improvement); early stopping patience 10; best‑epoch weights retained; convergence in ~30–40 epochs.\n",
    "\n",
    "Evaluation & Explainability\n",
    "\n",
    "Macro‑averaged F1 across classes; confusion‑matrix review by class support.\n",
    "\n",
    "Grad‑CAM overlays examined to validate saliency patterns against expected land‑use signatures."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d7b71834-ca2d-48f9-9f11-a9dba43a1a14",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Limitations"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "b04c437d-499c-40e7-a289-ade75af82731",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Label and support constraints: Some drivers remain under‑represented; several classes deemed non‑learnable at this resolution were excluded.\n",
    "\n",
    "Seasonality: Maize and other crops can appear very different depending on where they are in their harvesting sycle\n",
    "\n",
    "Sensor resolution: 30 m Landsat may blur fine‑scale features characteristic of smallholder activity."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6f9b8da2-4ad6-4425-bac1-462c756c803c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Repo contents"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "52fbb1cc-b5e5-412e-9f3a-3b3c5e8a9daa",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Main notebooks are as follows\n",
    "\n",
    "Model training and eval: Self explanatory\n",
    "Undisturbed forest class downloader: Demonstrates how to retrieve rainforest images from Google Earth engine\n",
    "EDA and cleaning. Contains most of the exploratory data analysis done to the original dataset provided by debus\n",
    "\n",
    "a helpers.py file also includes helper functions used mainly during EDA \n",
    "\n",
    "To retrieve the train-ready dataset follow this link https://drive.google.com/drive/u/1/folders/1pxGrQHesxhE5h0CbXHdRc7ZKIFx_hfqj"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "482c6cd6-2eaa-4010-9336-9c13ae63f261",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Summary "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "87ed3724-1b18-414e-a616-3f01938f96cb",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "A compact, open‑source based pipeline can produce actionable, driver‑level forest‑loss intelligence for the African rainforest. With impressive performance on a sparse dataset and room for improvement, this approach offers an efficient alternative to costly ground campaigns and a practical tool for allocating conservation resources."
   ]
  },
